        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add Control UI plugin management",
        "body": "Closes #103135\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's optional plugins are discoverable and manageable through CLI/config workflows, but the Control UI had no coherent place to see what is installed and running, enable a bundled capability such as Workboard, install or remove a ClawHub plugin, or connect lightweight MCP-based integrations.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis builds a full plugin manager at `/settings/plugins` on top of the existing plugin lifecycle, with two tabs:\n\n- **Installed** — the complete local inventory (141 plugins on a real gateway) grouped by category, flowing into two columns on wide layouts. A compact **inventory pulse** replaces stat cards: a segmented enabled/disabled/issues meter whose legend and counts live inside the filter chips. Every row opens a **detail overlay** (hero art, primary enable/install action, metadata table); an overflow (`…`) menu offers Enable/Disable, View details, and a confirm-guarded **Remove** for externally installed plugins. The tab also manages **MCP servers** inline (list, add via URL or command with inferred transport, enable/disable, remove) through the existing `config.patch` seam using minimal RFC 7396 merge patches; stdio rows show only the command since args can carry credentials.\n- **Discover** — the store: featured bundled plugins, official externals, and a **\"Connect your world\"** shelf of 28 connectors organized into use-case groups (Work & productivity, Coding & infrastructure, Home & media, Everyday life). One-click MCP connectors cover Notion, Linear, Todoist, Airtable, Canva, Stripe, GitHub, Sentry, Context7, DeepWiki, Hugging Face, and Home Assistant; curated ClawHub searches cover calendar, email, PDF, transcription, Jira, Grafana, Kubernetes, Spotify, Sonos, Reddit, stocks, flights, news, maps, translation, and notes. Typing in the search box queries ClawHub inline (through the gateway — anonymous, no account needed) and appends a **From ClawHub** section with download counts and source-verification badges; \"Browse ClawHub\" is a quiet header link there.\n\nEvery catalog entry renders **cover art**: 172 bundled 512px WebP illustrations (generated with Codex CLI, ~2.1MB under `ui/public/plugin-art/`) covering the full bundled inventory, every connector, and the store shelves, with deterministic gradient monogram tiles as the fallback for unknown ClawHub packages. The gateway CSP is `img-src 'self'`, so artwork ships with the bundle.\n\n**Connector vetting.** Every connector passed a three-stage subagent review: (1) official-docs verification plus live endpoint probes for MCP servers, (2) ClawHub result-quality and malware/typosquat screening for curated searches, and (3) an adversarial pass that dynamically registered OAuth clients to prove one-click viability. That review removed Figma (client-allowlisted registration, live 403) and Atlassian (upstream OAuth issuer-mismatch bug), downgraded GitHub to PAT-based setup (no dynamic client registration upstream), fixed the Linear endpoint (`/sse` retired → `/mcp`) and Home Assistant (`/api/mcp`, streamable HTTP), and dropped or retargeted searches whose top results were squatted by suspicious packages (a bulk-published wrapper cluster routing queries and API keys to a third-party service now sits on ClawHub's \"never highlight\" radar; details in the review artifacts).\n\nBackend additions (all additive, no protocol version bump):\n\n- `plugins.uninstall` (`operator.admin`, control-plane write): lock-guarded removal mirroring the CLI flow — config references, install record, managed files, registry refresh. Bundled plugins stay disable-only.\n- `PluginCatalogEntry` gains `category` (manifest-derived) and `removable`; search results gain `downloads` and `verificationTier`.\n- Catalog display metadata prefers manifest names/channel labels/blurbs over npm package specifiers (\"Telegram — simplest way to get started…\" instead of \"@openclaw/telegram\").\n- Hosted feed entries without a declared runtime id no longer pin `expectedPluginId` to their package name (which rejected every legitimate install), while explicitly declared ids stay enforced even when they equal the package name; installed packages now also suppress their hosted catalog rows.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperator admins get a single place to see what is installed and running, click into any plugin for details, enable/disable/remove via familiar store-style menus, install from the curated store or inline ClawHub search, and wire up vetted MCP connectors without touching JSON. Read-only operators can still browse and search with mutation controls disabled and explained.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm tsgo:all`, `pnpm test:ui` (i18n drift gate + 2,693 UI tests across 188 files), focused backend suites (protocol validators, management service incl. uninstall/removable/pin regression tests, gateway handlers, descriptor scopes), and the 3-scenario Chromium E2E all pass on Blacksmith Testbox.\n- The E2E covers the detail overlay, menu-driven enable and uninstall with confirm + page notice, unified inline ClawHub search with badges, connector cards, risk-ack retry, read-only blocking, list-failure retry, and mobile layout.\n- `pnpm build` passes including the production Control UI build; protocol schema/Swift generators are deterministic.\n- **Live gateway proof** (isolated `OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR` + sanitized env, this branch's build): browsed the 141-plugin inventory, installed `@openclaw/bluebubbles` from ClawHub through the UI and removed it via the menu flow, and added/removed MCP connectors with the config file verified after each step.\n- Mandatory autoreview (Codex, gpt-5.5, high) ran across four iterations; accepted findings — MCP transport defaults, RFC 7396 delete semantics, a runtime-id pin regression, duplicate hosted catalog rows after install, and Discover-tab error visibility — were each fixed with regression tests. Final run clean.\n\n### Screenshots (live gateway, this branch)\n\n#### Installed inventory: pulse header, two columns, full artwork (dark)\n\n![Installed inventory](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/installed-dark.png)\n\n![Inventory artwork](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/installed-artwork-dark.png)\n\n![Row actions menu](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/row-menu-dark.png)\n\n#### Plugin detail overlay\n\n![Detail overlay](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/detail-dark.png)\n\n#### Discover: featured shelf + grouped connectors (full page)\n\n![Discover full](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/discover-full-dark.png)\n\n#### Unified inline ClawHub search\n\n![Unified search](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/unified-search-dark.png)\n\n#### Light theme\n\n![Installed light](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/installed-light.png)\n\n![Discover light](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/discover-light.png)\n\n#### Mobile\n\n<img width=\"393\" alt=\"Discover mobile\" src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/pr-103176/discover-mobile.png\" />\n",
